es of rucking using an extra 10% of your bodyweight in a ruck or backpack. Adjust based on your current strength and conditioning levels. If you want to add daily walks on top of this, that can also work very well. Walking before eating in the morning may be ideal, but walking at any time of day can still support fat loss, recovery, and overall health. FAQ What supplements should I take? Whey protein isolate is always a solid option, as is a quality multivitamin . Creatine monohydrate is another great supplement for all adults, especially those over 40. 6 Other supplements worth considering include a joint support formula, essential amino acids , and magnesium . Can I add more to this? You can add more work if you feel you need it, but try to stay with similar sets and rep schemes. Keep in mind that adding more exercises will also increase the amount of time you spend training. Adjust your weekly schedule accordingly. What if I miss a workout? Just pick back up the next day and keep moving forward. Don’t worry about trying to make up a missed workout or doubling up in one day. Staying consistent over time matters far more. How much weight can I expect to lose? Many variables can influence how much weight or fat you lose, so it’s impossible to predict an exact number. However, most people following this program can aim for an initial goal of losing around 10 pounds in eight weeks. That would be both a healthy and meaningful rate of progress. References: Mobility training for increasing mobility and functioning in older people with frailty. Daniel Treacy 1, Leanne Hassett 2, Karl Schurr 3, Nicola J Fairhall 4, Ian D Cameron 5, Catherine Sherrington 4 Effectiveness of an intermittent fasting diet versus regular diet on fat loss in overweight and obese middle-aged and elderly people without metabolic disease: a systematic review and meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials. Ke Yao 1, Hao Su 2, Kaiyin Cui 1, Ye Gao 1, Dengyun Xu 1, Qian Wang 1, Zhitong Ha 1, Teng Zhang 1, Shuning Chen 1, Tao Liu 1 Full-body resistance training promotes greater fat mass loss than a split-body routine in well-trained males: A randomized trial. Marcelo A S Carneiro 1 2, Paulo Ricardo P Nunes 1 3, Markus V C Souza 1, Cláudio O Assumpção 1, Fábio L Orsatti 1 4 Aerobic exercise training at maximal fat oxidation intensity improves body composition, glycemic control, and physical capacity in older people with type 2 diabetes. Yan Jiang 1, Sijie Tan 1, Zhaoyu Wang 1, Zhen Guo 1, Qingwen Li 1, Jianxiong Wang 2 Effect of Aerobic or Resistance Exercise, or Both, on Intermuscular and Visceral Fat and Physical and Metabolic Function in Older Adults With Obesity While Dieting. Debra L Waters 1 2, Lina Aguirre 1 3, Burke Gurney 4, David R Sinacore 5 6, Kenneth Fowler 3, Giulia Gregori 7 8, Reina Armamento-Villareal 7 8, Clifford Qualls 9, Dennis T Villareal 7 8 Effectiveness of Creatine Supplementation on Aging Muscle and Bone: Focus on Falls Prevention and Inflammation. Darren G Candow 1,*, Scott C Forbes 2, Philip D Chilibeck 3, Stephen M Cornish 4, Jose Antonio 5, Richard B Kreider 6', PopularityRank=NULL, PopularityWindow=NULL,
