    VALUES (@ImportedMealSuggestionId, N'Low Carb Berry Cobbler Crumble Recipe', N'Breakfast', N'For a snack or desert that''s full of micro-nutrients and antioxidants, give this low carb berry crumble a try. This treat is both sweet and healthy!', 222, 11, 22, 10, NULL, 1, 10142, N'https://www.muscleandstrength.com/recipes/low-carb-berry-crumble', N'https://cdn.muscleandstrength.com/sites/default/files/field/feature-image/recipe/berry-crumble-feature.jpg', N'Makes 2-4 servings. Macros represent 1/3 of recipe', N'Preheat oven to 375 degrees F Toss berries with xanthum gum, lemon zest and any sweetener, if using Put berries in a cast iron skillet or oven safe dish Bake for 15 minutes While berries are baking, mix together almond flour, protein powder and 1 tbsp. melted coconut oil until crumbly. You can also add in 1-2 tbs of dry sweetener, if desired After 15 minutes, remove berries from the oven and top with crumble mixture Bake 3-5 minutes or until golden Serve topped with whipped cream or greek yogurt Notes: *You can use any combination of fruit you would like. *Xanthum gum can be replaced with 1 tbs cornstarch This not only makes a great dessert, but also breakfast or snack!', N'["Low Carb Recipes","Snack Recipes","Breakfast Recipes"]', N'{"calories_kcal":"222","protein_g":"11","carbs_g":"22","fat_g":"10"}', 15900);
