    SuggestedMonth=NULL, IsSystemDefault=1, SortOrder=10179, SourceUrl=N'https://www.muscleandstrength.com/recipes/black-forest-protein-brownies', ImageUrl=N'https://cdn.muscleandstrength.com/sites/default/files/field/feature-image/recipe/black-forest-brownies-feature.jpg', ServingSuggestion=N'Makes 8 brownies', ContentText=N'Preheat oven to 350 degrees F Spray an 8x8 glass baking dish with non stick spray Mix together milk, eggwhites, apple sauce and greek yogurt In a second bowl, whisk together oar flour, protein powder, sweetener, baking soda and cocoa powder Add 1/3 of dry ingredients to your wet ingredients Mix Add next 1/3 of dry ingredients Mix Add remaining dry ingredients and mix until just combined Allow batter to sit for 5 minutes Pour batter into baking dish Bake for about 20-25 minutes or until a toothpick comes out clean While brownies are baking, add greek yogurt, cherries and sweetener to a food processor Mix until just combined Notes: *You can substitute the chocolate egg whites for plain, however the chocolate flavor will be a bit more mild **Make sure you are using a thick greek yogurt, such as chobani, otherwise your ‘frosting’ will be runny. If your yogurt is thinner, you can fix this by adding in some vanilla protein powder (1tbs at a time) to reach your desired frosting like consistency and increase the protein content of the brownies.', CategoriesJson=N'["Snack Recipes"]', SourceMacrosJson=N'{"calories_kcal":"146","protein_g":"14","carbs_g":"22","fat_g":"2"}', ReadCount=11600
